-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Data.Relations: what each item is used for and where it comes from, IDs only
--
-- From the Lab's big dump of build 70448 (/recollect-data rebuilds this file;
-- do not edit it by hand). Names, titles and descriptions are read live in
-- the player's language. Each bucket (item ID // 1024) is one string of
-- records: byte 30, the item ID, byte 31, its codes joined by ";" (the
-- codes are listed in Facts/Relations.lua). Q holds quest frequencies
-- (d daily, w weekly, y yearly, r repeatable, q world quest, m monthly) the
-- same way by quest ID; C the recipes whose schematics the Lab read, bucketed by
-- spell ID: "skillLine,product item,quantity". M holds the item that teaches each
-- mount, by the mount's spell (AllTheThings), so a mount link finds its item.
-- J holds the Encounter Journal encounter each boss a drop names is, bucketed by NPC ID.
-- T holds the item behind each ensemble (e), weapon illusion (l), pet species (p) and
-- recipe spell (r) a purchase names: T.e[set] = item.
-- G holds where each quest a code names starts, bucketed by quest ID like Q:
-- "npc/npc,map,x,y" (x and y in thousandths; every giver, the one standing at
-- that place first; npc 0 when no giver is known).
-- Z holds who takes each quest's turn-in, bucketed like G: "npc/npc" ascending
-- (accepted curator findings; G says only where a quest starts).
-- F holds the other qualities of an item (the same thing in another quality, data format 12),
-- bucketed by item ID: "item,item" ascending, every item of the family but this one.
-- L holds the encounters whose loot comes out of each boss loot chest, bucketed
-- by object ID: "encounter,encounter" ascending (AllTheThings).
-- W holds what each quest a use code names rewards, bucketed by quest ID: things
-- typed as a purchase's are ("p3389" a pet species, a plain item by its ID), ","
-- between them, "k" before a choice. K holds what a combine's product is when it
-- is a collectible: K[item] = "p3389". X holds the patch in which every route to
-- an item was removed from the game, bucketed by item ID: "120100" (12.1.0), or
-- "120100,120001" with the patch it was added (AllTheThings). A holds the patch an
-- item still in the game was added in, bucketed like X, where that patch's expansion
-- is later than the one the game files the item under (AllTheThings).
-- S holds each profession's recipe spells, by skill line: "spell,spell" ascending
-- (the recipes the Lab read and AllTheThings' recipe list), for curator mode.
-- H holds the meta achievements each achievement counts toward, bucketed by its ID:
-- "meta,meta" ascending (the dump's achievement criteria of type 8); I the reverse,
-- each meta's achievements, bucketed by the meta's ID.
-- N lists the items Data/Secrets.lua's secrets use (made, taken, used or chosen
-- among), ascending, so they read Can't tell while that file can't be read.
-- dataVersion and format are the data build's stamp; Vendors.lua and Hints.lua
-- carry the same one (Facts/DataVersion.lua reads the data only when they agree).
